---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_EMAIL, AUTHOR_GITHUB } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Norberto Gomez Jr — mechatronics engineer working in UAV ground operations, writing first-principles notes on how things work."
>
	<div class="prose" style="padding-top: 1.5rem;">
		<h2 style="margin-top: 0;">About</h2>

		<p>
			I'm Norberto — a mechatronics engineer in McKinney, Texas. I work in
			ground operations for autonomous UAVs, which in practice means scheduled
			maintenance, ground control stations, firmware, field deployments, and
			working out why something that ran fine yesterday doesn't today.
		</p>

		<p>
			Before that I built and commissioned automated production machinery for
			battery manufacturing in Ireland, ran a production floor, and spent
			several years in regulated medical manufacturing. I hold a BEng in
			Mechatronics from Atlantic Technological University.
		</p>

		<p>
			This blog is where I write things down — mostly the things I work with or
			want to understand properly: electricity, motors, sensors, control loops,
			machines, cars, and lately the silicon underneath modern computing. Some
			software too.
		</p>

		<p>
			The rule I try to hold to is <em>no hand-waving</em>. If an explanation
			bottoms out at "and then it just works," it isn't finished. Most posts
			start from one physical fact and build up from there, because that's the
			only way I've ever managed to actually remember anything.
		</p>

		<p>
			A few of them run as connected series: <a
				href="/blog/how-electricity-actually-works/">Maker Basics</a
			> on electronics from the ground up, <a
				href="/blog/the-loops-that-drive-your-car/">Under the Hood</a
			> on how cars work, and <a href="/blog/what-a-transistor-actually-does/"
				>Inside the Machine</a
			> on the hardware AI runs on. The <a href="/projects/">projects page</a> has
			things I've actually built; my <a href="/cv/">CV</a> has the professional version.
		</p>

		<p class="about-contact">
			<a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR_EMAIL}`}>{AUTHOR_EMAIL}</a>
			<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
			<a href={AUTHOR_GITHUB} rel="me">GitHub</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
